 "subtitles": {
  "intro": {
   "text": "Twenty-seven instruments in here, and not one of them tells you what it is. ? pick one up before you read its label — can you say what it does ?",
   "speaker": "The bench",
   "level": 1
  },
  "ask_add": {
   "text": "? walk a, then walk b — where do you end up ?",
   "speaker": "Addition",
   "level": 1
  },
  "truth_add": {
   "text": "At a + b. To add is to walk, not to count. ? now stand at b and look back at a — what are you looking along ?",
   "speaker": "Addition",
   "level": 1
  },
  "truth_sub": {
   "text": "a − b, the arrow from b back to a. Every “where is it, from here” is a subtraction. ? make an arrow twice as long — did it turn ?",
   "speaker": "Subtraction",
   "level": 1
  },
  "truth_scale": {
   "text": "No. A scalar is a volume knob for a direction — length and direction come apart. ? hold two arrows and turn one until the number peaks ?",
   "speaker": "Scale",
   "level": 1
  },
  "truth_dot": {
   "text": "a·b = |a||b|cos θ — agreement, written as a number. ? keep turning past zero and watch the other gauge — what grows as the agreement dies ?",
   "speaker": "Dot product",
   "level": 1
  },
  "truth_cross": {
   "text": "The turn left over when two directions refuse to align, standing at right angles to both. ? stand an arrow in the light — is its shadow shorter than the arrow ?",
   "speaker": "Cross product",
   "level": 1
  },
  "close": {
   "text": "It is. That shadow is the projection — the part of you that lives along someone else's line. Seven operations, laid out in a row like a shop. ? who decided these seven were the operations ?",
   "speaker": "The bench",
   "level": 1
  }
 },
